  "notes": "GOLD v1 fix (round 1) of sc_c27168a2de83 (28289002_B01.ply, part 28289002, FULL, CAD bend lines 3; custody CONSUMED, BENCHMARK_V3 scans[36]). Started from benchmark_v3/label_lines/sc_c27168a2de83/pairs.json. Part: Z-profile stepped channel bracket, t~1.48 mm. Profile: tabbed wall 3/4, then a ~37 deg fold into the sloped chamfer band 5/8/9, then a ~53 deg fold (same turning direction) into the perforated base 1/7, then a 90 deg fold turning the opposite way into the short wall 2/6 (~99 mm, between relief notches). Base skin 1 is concave at B2 but convex at B3. All three folds are parallel within ~0.15 deg and straight lengthwise. Exactly 3 formed folds, matching the CAD count. The tabs on wall 3 are coplanar with the wall. Holes, slots, relief notches, thickness/end edges and arc facets 10/11 are not bends. Fix: B2 was on the inner (concave) skin [5,1], 1.47 mm off the outer apex (3/3 auditors). It is now rebuilt on the outer skins: chamfer outside [8,9] and base outside [7], with an explicit extent over the full fold. The auto extent clips to ~26 mm because 7 only covers one end. The outer arc is scanned over t~-68.6..-2 (11 plus unsegmented points). Over the rest the fold is evidenced by the inner arc 10 and skins 5/1, which run straight and one thickness inward. B1 and B3 are unchanged (3/3 auditors OK).",
